{"date": "2026-09-17", "title": "Pop Culture Digest — Thursday, September 17, 2026", "link": "https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-17/", "pubDate": "Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:00:00 -0500", "description": "\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"background:#f4f1ec;\">\n<tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:28px 12px;\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"600\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"max-width:600px;width:100%;background:#ffffff;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;\">\n  <tr><td style=\"background:#111111;padding:28px 28px 22px;color:#fff;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c9a66b;\">Weekday morning</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;margin-top:8px;font-weight:normal;\">Pop Culture Digest</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#d0d0d0;margin-top:8px;\">Thursday, September 17, 2026 · Movies, TV, music & streaming</div>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:18px 28px 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:#444;\">\n    Six fresh stories to start the day: a video-game reboot that critics are calling historic, two Netflix trailers with serious star power, two big series drops today, and a Tove Lo album arriving tomorrow.\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 1 Resident Evil -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:20px 28px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9a3412;font-weight:600;\">Movies</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 12px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Zach Cregger’s <em>Resident Evil</em> opens at 97% on Rotten Tomatoes</h2>\n    <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-17/images/img1.jpg\" alt=\"Resident Evil film still\" width=\"544\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:544px;height:auto;border-radius:4px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:14px 0 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">Critics are treating the <em>Weapons</em> director’s Capcom reinvention like a breakthrough. Early reviews put it at 97% Fresh — the highest-rated live-action video-game movie on Rotten Tomatoes — with GamesRadar calling it “the best video game movie full stop.” It opens in theaters tomorrow, September 18.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;\"><a href=\"https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/horror-movies/zach-creggers-resident-evil-debuts-to-97-percent-on-rotten-tomatoes-making-it-the-highest-rated-live-action-video-game-adaptation-ever/\" style=\"color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline;\">Read the GamesRadar report →</a></p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 2 Sacrifice -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 28px 8px;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#1d4ed8;font-weight:600;\">Streaming</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 12px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Anya Taylor-Joy wants to throw Chris Evans into a volcano in <em>Sacrifice</em></h2>\n    <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-17/images/img2.jpg\" alt=\"Sacrifice trailer still with Chris Evans\" width=\"544\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:544px;height:auto;border-radius:4px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:14px 0 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">Netflix dropped the trailer for Romain Gavras’s dark adventure-comedy: Evans plays a fading action star hijacked at an environmental gala by Taylor-Joy’s radical cult leader, who thinks a volcanic sacrifice will save the planet. Charli XCX and Yung Lean pop up too. It streams October 16.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RDJ2R-1tvW0\" style=\"color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline;\">Watch the official trailer →</a></p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 3 Animals -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 28px 8px;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#1d4ed8;font-weight:600;\">Streaming</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 12px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Ben Affleck and Kerry Washington race a ransom clock in <em>Animals</em></h2>\n    <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-17/images/img3.jpg\" alt=\"Animals trailer still\" width=\"544\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:544px;height:auto;border-radius:4px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:14px 0 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">Affleck directs and stars as an L.A. mayoral candidate whose son is kidnapped — just as most of the family’s money is locked in the campaign. Washington plays his wife; Gillian Anderson and Steven Yeun round out the ensemble. The full trailer is out; the thriller hits Netflix October 9.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3WJw6BB7m_E\" style=\"color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline;\">Watch the Animals trailer →</a></p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 4 Monster -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 28px 8px;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7c3aed;font-weight:600;\">TV</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 12px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\"><em>Monster: The Lizzie Borden Story</em> is live — first woman at the center of the anthology</h2>\n    <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-17/images/img4.jpg\" alt=\"Monster The Lizzie Borden Story\" width=\"544\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:544px;height:auto;border-radius:4px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:14px 0 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">Ryan Murphy and Ian Brennan’s true-crime anthology returns with Ella Beatty as Lizzie Borden, alongside Charlie Hunnam, Rebecca Hall, and Vicky Krieps. It’s the series’ first female-focused season, framing the 1892 Fall River axe murders through repression, rage, and American folklore. Now streaming on Netflix.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;\"><a href=\"https://www.netflix.com/tudum/articles/monster-season-4-lizzie-borden-release-date-cast-news\" style=\"color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline;\">Read the Netflix Tudum overview →</a></p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 5 Stranger Things -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 28px 8px;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7c3aed;font-weight:600;\">TV</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 12px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\"><em>Stranger Things: Tales From ’85</em> Season 2 drops today</h2>\n    <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-17/images/img5.jpg\" alt=\"Stranger Things Tales From 85\" width=\"544\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:544px;height:auto;border-radius:4px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:14px 0 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">The animated Hawkins Investigators Club is back for Valentine’s Day — and a wave of iridescent flowers that are anything but romantic. Season 2 premieres today with eight episodes, ghostly apparitions, hate sprites, and a mine the gang has never explored. Jeremy Jordan voices Steve Harrington among the returning adults.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;\"><a href=\"https://www.netflix.com/tudum/articles/stranger-things-tales-from-85-season-2-release-date\" style=\"color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline;\">Catch the Season 2 trailer &amp; details →</a></p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <!-- 6 Tove Lo -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 28px 8px;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#be185d;font-weight:600;\">Music</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 12px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Tove Lo’s <em>ESTRUS</em> lands tomorrow — “a lot of feelings, no solutions”</h2>\n    <img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-09-17/images/img6.jpg\" alt=\"Tove Lo\" width=\"544\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:544px;height:auto;border-radius:4px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:14px 0 8px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\">The Swedish pop star’s sixth album arrives September 18 via Pretty Swede / Virgin, with Stromae on “des fleurs” and a world tour already underway (Chicago was last night). She describes the record as primal and unresolved — childhood summers, breakups, and bodies that want different things than minds. Cue it up tonight.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;\"><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/album/6di14tEch7EQ0jMglRwcf6\" style=\"color:#0b57d0;text-decoration:underline;\">Open ESTRUS on Spotify →</a></p>\n  </td></tr>\n\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px;border-top:1px solid #eee;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#777;\">\n    You’re getting this weekday Pop Culture Digest because you asked for it. Sent from popculture@agentmail.to · Links go to trailers, streaming pages, and source reporting.\n  </td></tr>\n</table>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n"}